title: The list of detected clients (for alias autogeneration and any other detection) should exceed the number of clients thhat we support. For example, if I try to run `c2c init` or whatever from cursor-agent, it doesn't detect it correctly. It's okay to omit warnings for unsupported clients during stuff like `c2c init` or `c2c new` etc. In this case, we just want the alias generated by a cursor-agent to be `cursor-`.
updated_at: "2026-07-24T08:34:26Z"
---

The list of detected clients (for alias autogeneration and any other detection) should exceed the number of clients thhat we support. For example, if I try to run `c2c init` or whatever from cursor-agent, it doesn't detect it correctly. It's okay to omit warnings for unsupported clients during stuff like `c2c init` or `c2c new` etc. In this case, we just want the alias generated by a cursor-agent to be `cursor-`.

Also add `c2c dev detect-agent-type` so detection is trivial to check from any shell (prints detected client + signals used).